# Tesla Model 3 four-door saloon, 2017 onwards.
#
# The compact electric saloon: the smooth closed nose, the flush door
# handles, the full-glass roof and the short boot. UK orders opened 1 May
# 2019. The 2023-24 Highland facelift changed the lamps, nose and tail and is
# a colour-run change on the same shell; the pre-facelift car is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tesla_Model_3
#
# Dimensions 4.694 x 1.849 x 1.443 m, wheelbase 2.875 m (2017-23 car).
#
# Shape reference: the pack's images show the pre-facelift car in side,
# front and rear views; the side view governs.
#
# Colours: grade (c) for Red Multi-Coat and Deep Blue Metallic, the colours
# named in the Autocar first-delivery report of June 2019; grade (d) for Pearl
# White, Solid Black and Midnight Silver. Weights 20, 18, 17, 15, total 70,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 225 km/h. Comfort 90/315, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 90: a quiet
# electric cabin with a glass roof. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 2019 intro, retires staggered 2042-2045.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/tesla-model-3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/tesla-model-3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/tesla-model-3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pre-facelift body throughout, ends included. The lamp
# internals, the alloy spokes and the panel seams are simplified.


obj=citycar
name=TeslaModel3(PearlWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=20
intro_year=2019
intro_month=5
retire_year=2045
retire_month=6
speed=225
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=315

